  "query_preview": "/Friday through Wednesday/... \nLarge scale troughing will remain situated over our region on\nFriday with even one or two decent shortwaves moving through the\nregion, but little will result from their passage. Enough dry air\nwill have already moved into the area to essentially prevent any\nadditional rain chances across the lower deserts on Friday to at\nmost a 10-15% chance over the eastern Arizona high terrain. The\ncooler air mass settling in will also keep daytime highs only in\nthe mid to upper 70s Friday. Model guidance suggests the trough\nshould remain over our region even through the upcoming weekend,\nbut it will continue to weaken with our air mass slowly warming\nover time. NBM forecast highs for Sunday show readings into the \nlower 80s over the western lower deserts to near 80 degrees in the\nPhoenix area. By Monday, the trough is likely to finally push \neast of the region with modest upper level ridging prevailing over\nthe Desert Southwest. The increased heights and continued dry \nconditions should push daytime highs back into the normal range \n(mid 80s) going into the middle of next week.",
